Make UNSLOTH_FORCE_FLOAT32=1 actually run float32 (was silently fp16).

Both _autocast_dtype initializers in rl_replacements.py handled
UNSLOTH_FORCE_FLOAT32=1 by setting the autocast dtype to torch.float16 -
the exact opposite of the requested full-precision compute. The zoo copy
(unsloth_zoo/rl_replacements.py) gets this right by setting None.

Setting None alone is not enough here: torch.amp.autocast(dtype=None) on
CUDA falls back to the device default (fp16 again), so every consumer of
self._autocast_dtype also gains enabled = self._autocast_dtype is not None,
which turns the context manager into a no-op (true float32) when forced.
The dtype_bytes accounting already anticipated None (else-branch = 32).
